{
 "comment": "#624 L1b, the regression against master (plans/624.md 10.2; gate.sh baseline-scenes, then render.py --compare, max 0 on every image): with the knee chosen (metal_light_hdr 2), with the setting set and no rig or a rig that is off, and across toggles, a render is master's bit for bit. knee_<rep>_rt<n>: a 2-light rig (a warm spot at intensity 2 and a fill, highlights on) at metal_light_hdr 2 on cartoon, surface, sticks, spheres, the bezier tube (lighting_613's CGO), the 50% transparent surface (oit50), the glass surface, metallic spheres (rt1: the RT rig composite with reflections) and cartoon with organic sticks under a shadowed spot (shadow); knee_air: haze 0.3 and dust 0.5 at full resolution (rt0, rt1) and half (airhalf); knee_tonemap: metal_exposure 0.7 and metal_tonemap 1 with the rig on. norig_hdr1 (rig none, the setting 1), norig_hdrjunk (7), rigoff_hdr1 (the harness's --rig off path), norig_tonemap (#13's exposure 0.7 and ACES with no rig, the setting 1). toggle_surface: each run installs the rig at HDR and forces a frame (cmd.png, 320x180, the system temp dir), then the harness turns the rig off. flip_knee: each run forces a frame at metal_light_hdr 1 with the rig on, then sets 2 before the export. metal_light_hdr is set only through _l624_opt (it exists from #624 part 2), so master renders this file natively; every other line runs on master. Same cmd.set_lights shim as lighting_624.json (rigs with an explicit centre and size, the extent of m). metal_light_air_time is pinned at 2.0. FROZEN: master's renders are keyed on this file's sha. Checked in CI by testing/tests/raymol/lighting_hdr_check.py.",
 "base": null,
 "rig": "on",
 "size": [
  1280,
  720
 ],
 "extra": [
  "import math as _l624_math",
  "import os as _l624_os",
